{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And it will consume them this instant.</b> And if you ask: but it is established for us that He does not punish unless He has first warned. Rather, Moses said to him in the name of HaKadosh Baruch Hu: 'Be before YHWH tomorrow, you and Aharon.' And he did not do so, but rather 'he assembled against them all the people' — therefore He was immediately angered at them. But below, regarding 'separate yourselves from the midst of the assembly' — there they had already been warned."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:18:16.574310858Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}